Z||000000||tomanyfieros||10-14-2001||08:58 PM||||if it is 123456, where is #1 and where does it go? does that make sense? LMK<BR>Thanx JAson<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/dreamer.gif">    <BR><B>We all have dreams, but not everyone gets them...</B>||||reg||1
Z||000001||jelly2m8||10-15-2001||12:20 AM||||Cylinder number 1 is the one on the trunk side, nearest the alternator / belt.<P> IF ........notice  I state IF!!...........<P>  If the distributer rotor is in the same position it was originally installed from the factory, number 1 on the  cap is the terminal just behind the cap hold down screw closest to the plenum near the vacuum fitting.<P> If this doesnt work, you will need to put the engine at no.1 TDC on the compression stroke, pull the cap, and see which terminal the rotor is pointing at.<P>the firing order on the cap is 123456 clockwise.<P>the cylinders are numbered<P>-----------6 4 2--------------<BR>tranny---------------waterpump<BR>-----------5 3 1--------------<P>[This message has been edited by jelly2m8 (edited 10-15-2001).]<p>[This message has been edited by jelly2m8 (edited 10-15-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||tgowens||10-15-2001||12:56 AM||||or..........another way of looking at it is.. when the engine is at Top Dead Center (compression on #1 cylinder) the rotor should point at the 8mm screw on the plenum......then when you replace the distributor cap #1 is the terminal right above the rotor blade........if you had the distributor out then this is a very important step when reinstalling it - otherwise you may be one tooth off and not be able to set the timing (as in the distributor won't rotate far enough to set the timing)- If that is the case, pull the dist. out and move it one tooth around and set it in again.....takes a little practice but I'm sure you can get it......<P>Otherwise, jelly2m8 is correct (and from his sig it appears that he has more wires than you do!)<P>Now that I have confused you.......||||reg||1
Z||000003||tomanyfieros||10-15-2001||07:08 AM||||                Rear window<BR>                  #6 # 4  #2<P>                  #5  #3  #1<BR>                    trunk<BR>is that right? LMK<BR>Thanx Jason||||reg||1
Z||000004||Wolfhound||10-15-2001||07:26 AM||||Right!||||reg||1
